  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "What it works out",
      "items": [
        "S_xy[k] = (1/blocks) * sum over b of X_b[k] * conj(Y_b[k])",
        "C[k] = |S_xy[k]|^2 / (S_xx[k] * S_yy[k]), which reads 0 to 1",
        "The angle of S_xy rising steadily with frequency is a delay"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "How the library gets there",
      "items": [
        "Both signals are cut and windowed the same way, then averaged as psd does",
        "Every correction of the window and the rate cancels in the ratio",
        "A bin where one signal holds nothing is set to zero, not divided by almost nothing"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "What will catch you",
      "items": [
        "Coherence of ONE block is always 1, because a number divided by itself is one",
        "Two peaks at 50 hertz prove nothing; half a building has one",
        "Coherence says whether the two peaks move together"
      ]
    }
  ]
